1490404549986124, -0.008868158794939518, 0.008427583612501621, 0.016452355310320854, 0.004619750659912825, 0.0034301963169127703, -0.02661077119410038, 0.0002983720041811466, 0.02240641973912716, -0.01706916093826294, -0.01248717401176691, 0.01246199756860733, 0.004443520680069923, -0.026635946705937386, -0.001335101667791605, 0.00010532512533245608, 0.006835217121988535], "index": 8, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7281, "total_tokens": 7281}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 2671 ---\nComponent: Object Store\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Role-based service bindings on Azure\nDescription: Object Store Service now supports read and write role based service binding credentials. Please refer the section Role-based Bindings and Service-keys for more details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-02\nValid as Of: 2024-07-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2672 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Discontinuation of btp CLI Client Versions 2.33 and older\nDescription: As announced on December 14, 2023, we have now discontinued client versions 2.33 and older.  Action: If you're still using one of these versions, you need to update to the latest btp CLI client version from: SAP Development Tools as these versions can no longer be used. See Get Updates for the btp CLI.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2673 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Error Message for Non-Assigned Roles\nDescription: We've reworked the information screen that is shown if no roles are assigned for a user.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2674 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.7.0\nDescription:   This release contains Istio in version 1.21.3. For more details, read Istio 1.21.3 Release Announcement and Change Notes. See the changelog.  Now, you can opt out of the <ENABLE_EXTERNAL_NAME_ALIAS> Istio pilot environment variable in the Istio custom resource. This allows for retaining behavior that was present in Istio prior to version 1.21. See Istio Custom Resource Annotations.  We've added Request Authentication UI for Kyma dashboard.  Istio Operator does not restart Pods with the Istio sidecar that contain custom image annotations. See Resource Annotations.  We've changed Istio Ingress Gateway's scaling to be based only on CPU utilization. This adjustment ensures that the scaling is more responsive to traffic changes, as the Istio Ingress Gateway memory utilization is not a good indicator of the traffic load.  The default number of Istio Ingress Gateway replicas in smaller clusters is now set to 1.  We've introduced the compatibility mode, which allows you to mitigate breaking changes when a new Istio module's release introduces an Istio upgrade. The Istio module supports compatibility with the previous minor version of Istio. See Compatibility Mode.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-17\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2675 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Improved ML Models for Invoice, Purchase Order, and Payment Advice.\nDescription: We’ve improved the machine learning models for the document types invoice, purchase order, and payment advice.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-07-01\nValid as Of: 2024-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2676 ---\nComponent: Platform Domains\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: TLS 1.3 Support\nDescription: TLS 1.3, the latest version of the security protocol, brings significant improvements over TLS 1.2 by offering enhanced security, better performance, and increased privacy. Consequently, TLS 1.3 is planned to be enabled for all platform domains in the Neo environment by the end of June 2024. Furthermore, TLS 1.2 remains as a fallback option.  The following domains are adjusted:      *.<Region.Domain>      *.dispatcher.<Region.Domain>      *.cert.<Region.Domain>      *.static.<Region.Domain>      connectivitynotification.<Region.Domain>      connectivitytunnel.<Region.Domain>      For more information, see SAP Note 3435199 .  Action: During the transition period, until TLS 1.3 is fully enabled by the end of June 2024, we recommend you verify your clients by connecting them to the following URL (applicable for TLS 1.3 and TLS 1.2): https://account.ca1.hana.ondemand.com/#/home/welcome.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-02\nValid as Of: 2024-06-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2677 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   General availability of SAP Translation Hub in the BTP multi-environment   \nDescription:   SAP Translation Hub is now generally available in the BTP multi-environment (e.g. Cloud Foundry).   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-30\nValid as Of: 2024-06-30\nVersion: Cloud", ": SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   General availability of SAP Translation Hub in the BTP multi-environment   \nDescription:   SAP Translation Hub is now generally available in the BTP multi-environment (e.g. Cloud Foundry).   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-30\nValid as Of: 2024-06-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2678 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Israel (Tel Aviv)\nDescription: Israel (Tel Aviv) (cf-il30) is available as a new region running on Google Cloud for use with enterprise accounts. See Regions and API Endpoints Available for the Cloud Foundry Environment.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-28\nValid as Of: 2024-06-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2679 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Bureau van Dijk is now Moody's\nDescription: The credit product Orbis is now provided by Moody's. We've adjusted our documentation and user interface accordingly.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-28\nValid as Of: 2024-06-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2680 ---\nComponent: Cloud Management Tools,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Cost Information Added to the SAP BTPEA / CPEA Card in Costs and Usage Page\nDescription: In the Costs and Usage page in SAP BTP cockpit, the SAP BTP Enterprise Agreement (SAP BTPEA) and Cloud Platform Enterprise Agreement (CPEA) cards now display monthly cost information relating to your cloud credits for the current contract phase.  Use the card's new Costs and Usage buttons to switch between usage and cost information.   Note that this information was already available in the card's expanded view; we've promoted the information to the card's unexpanded view.  See Monitoring Usage and Consumption Costs in Your Global Account.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-27\nValid as Of: 2024-06-27\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 2951 ---\nComponent: Process Visibility Capability\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configure Sub-Status\nDescription: You can categorize scenario instances based on step information by configuring sub-status using the Step Information expression.  See Configure Status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2952 ---\nComponent: Process Visibility Capability\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Current Step Attributes\nDescription: You can now define calculated attributes to retrieve processor and recipients for active steps.  See Attributes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2953 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process Visibility - Configure Sub-Status\nDescription: You can categorize scenario instances based on step information by configuring sub-status using the Step Information expression.See Configure Status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2954 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process Visibility - Current Step Attributes\nDescription: You can now define calculated attributes to retrieve processor and recipients for active steps.See Attributes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2955 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Process Visibility - Trigger Process Action\nDescription: You can configure Trigger Process action in the visibility scenario to handle escalations flows.  See Trigger Process Action.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-15\nValid as Of: 2024-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2956 ---\nComponent: SAP Digital Payments Add-On\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP Help Portal content available in additional languages\nDescription: The SAP Help Portal content is now available in the following languages:      English      French      German    Japanese  Portuguese (Brazil)    Russian    Simplified Chinese  Spanish  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2957 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Labels Claim, Release, Forward Are Now Consistent for All Task Providers\nDescription: The labels for the actions Claim, Release, and Forward are now defined by the SAP Task Center Web app and are consistent for all task providers. For more informaiton, see Working with the Task List > Inline Decision Options and Predefined Decision Reasons.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-14\nValid as Of: 2024-05-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2958 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Updated Icons for SAP Concur and SAP Fieldglass\nDescription: The icons for SAP Concur and SAP Fieldglass in the filter tabs of the SAP Task Center Web app are now updated. For more information, see Configure Filter Tabs in the SAP Task Center Web App.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-14\nValid as Of: 2024-05-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2959 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enrichment Data API - Deprecation of the Endpoint: Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous)\nDescription: The Enrichment Data API endpoint Delete Enrichment Data (Synchronous) is now deprecated and scheduled for decommissioning in February 2025. Following that date, the endpoint will no longer be available.  Please use the endpoint Delete Enrichment Data to delete data records.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-14\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2960 ---\nComponent: Edge Integration Cell\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Edge Integration Cell is now supported on Google Cloud Platform\nDescription: You can now activate the Edge Integration Cell runtime within your SAP Integration Suite tenant on Google Cloud Platform.  See: Activate Edge Integration Cell\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-13\nValid as Of: 2024-05-13\nVersion: 2403\n\n", "--- Record 2861 ---\nComponent: Data Quality Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Enhancements\nDescription:   The service is now available in the US East region (cf-us10) on Amazon Web Service (AWS).   Improvements were made to geocoding in Japan.   The new DQMMICRO_VIEWER role allows users to view information in the UI but not change it.   \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2862 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Unified Access Control Settings\nDescription: The access control settings have been aligned across all workspace screens and offer the same access options:  Specific users or user lists.  Specific roles (for site admins).  All internal users.  All external users (when enabled).  All users.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-16\nValid as Of: 2024-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2863 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Workspace Clickable Menu\nDescription: For a clickable workspace menu item, the company admin can decide whether to render the workspace with a header or not:  When a workspace header is rendered, workpages in the workspace navigation bar will be expanded as a vertical sub menu (no change).  When a workspace header is not rendered, when clicking the workspace menu item, all workspace navigation bar items will be displayed with an horizontal layout, (similar as 'My Workspace').  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-16\nValid as Of: 2024-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2864 ---\nComponent: SAP Cloud Application Event Hub\nEnvironment: Other\nTitle: Event Connectivity service plan\nDescription: Consume SAP business events published to SAP Event Broker using an SAP Integration Suite tenant with an integration flow that exposes a webhook URL endpoint. See SAP Integration Suite as a Consumer.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-23\nValid as Of: 2024-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2865 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with new credit agency: Creditsafe\nDescription: The credit agency Creditsafe is now connected to SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for credit integration.   More information:  Available Credit Agency Products and Features    Your Tasks for Integrating a New Credit Agency  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-23\nValid as Of: 2024-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2866 ---\nComponent: SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New entity available for the Credit Integration Service API\nDescription: In our Credit Integration Service API, the new entity Latest Credit Report is available. Use it to receive the latest credit report of a credit agency in XML or JSON format.   More information: Latest Credit Report  (Log on with your SAP ID to access this document.)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-23\nValid as Of: 2024-05-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2867 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Handling Third-Party Cookies\nDescription: Storage Access API is now available for all SAP Cloud Identity Services tenants.  Action: We recommend you to test your application. For more information on Third-Party Cookies Deprecation. See Handling Third Party Cookies Deprecation in Identity Authentication and Testing Your Solution For Breakage.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-22\nValid as Of: 2024-05-22\nVersion: 26120\n\n--- Record 2868 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Handling rate limits for Microsoft Entra ID read operations\nDescription: Microsoft Entra ID source and proxy provisioning systems are now enhanced to support retry for a failed operation due to occurred exception 'Too many requests (429)'.   Previously, this option was possible only for the Microsoft Entra ID target system.  See Handle Failed Operations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-22\nValid as Of: 2024-05-22\nVersion: 26120\n\n--- Record 2869 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Logos\nDescription: You can use  files for your images in the administration console. See Upload Logo in Administration Console and Configure Tenant Images.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-22\nValid as Of: 2024-05-22\nVersion: 26120\n\n--- Record 2870 ---\nComponent: Cloud", "Environment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Logos\nDescription: You can use  files for your images in the administration console. See Upload Logo in Administration Console and Configure Tenant Images.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-22\nValid as Of: 2024-05-22\nVersion: 26120\n\n--- Record 2870 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Manage Applications\nDescription: Administrators with Manage Applications role and users with assigned authorization policies for read applications can see all applications in the tenant regardless of their Organization ID. See Edit Applications.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-22\nValid as Of: 2024-05-22\nVersion: 26120\n\n", "--- Record 881 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New HTTP Header for Client IP Address\nDescription: Beginning with this release, a new HTTP header called X-Cf-True-Client-Ip is automatically added to each HTTP request. This header contains the IP address of the client connecting to SAP BTP through the platform’s load balancer. The value of the header is a single IP address which can be utilized for IP address-based request filtering on the application side, such as per-client rate limiting and allow- or blocklisting clients by their IP addresses.  The HTTP header can also be used in conjunction with a route service, as the original client IP address is preserved in this scenario.  The header value is logged with the same key name X-Cf-True-Client-Ip by Gorouter for all incoming requests, allowing filtering and charting RTR logs by the client IP address.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 882 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 48.9.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 48.5.0 to 48.9.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.9.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.8.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.7.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.6.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 883 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Default Navigation When No Permissions\nDescription: Previously, when a user didn’t have permission to access a menu item, the user was redirected to the home page.   Now, the user will be redirected to the first main menu item that is accessible to the user (from left to right).   If a user doesn't have permission to access any menu items, the user will be redirected to a feed page under the company home.  Customers that prefer to keep the previous behavior (redirect to the home page), can add a menu workpage with the same content as the home page and grant users permission to access it.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-15\nVersion: 2504B\n\n--- Record 884 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: UX Improvements to the Transport Manager\nDescription: The following changes have been made to what was previously called the Transport Manager:  The Transport Manager is now called the Import Monitor.  The icon to open the Import Monitor has changed.  A strip message has been added explaining what the Import Monitor does.   