r create has been changed.  Previously, Identity Provisioning used to update the resolved users and to provision new users into the target system. After the change, Identity Provisioning updates only users resolved by userName in the target system, while the rest of the users are marked as skipped.  For more information, see Transformation Expressions → skipOperations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: 26936\n\n--- Record 1986 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Increased Maximum OIDC Token Validity\nDescription: With this release, we have increased the maximum validity of access and ID tokens for OpenID Connect applications from 1 hour to 12 hours. The default validity remains 1 hour.  For more information , see Tenant OpenID Connect Configurations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: 26936\n\n--- Record 1987 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Password Recovery\nDescription: You can enable or disable the option to reset the user password via an email link. See Enable Users to Recover Password via Email.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: 26936\n\n--- Record 1988 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: 26936\n\n--- Record 1989 ---\nComponent: Data Attribute Recommendation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: AI API - Regression Mode